  .target span{display:none}
  .target strong{font-size:24px}
  .board{--tile:52px; min-height:60px}
  .tile{font-size:22px}
  .operators{gap:10px}
  .op{width:44px;border-radius:14px;font-size:20px}
  .actions{gap:6px}
  .action{min-height:32px;padding:6px 12px;font-size:8px}
  .expression{min-height:16px;font-size:11px}
  .message{font-size:10px;min-height:14px}
  .footnote{display:none}
  .timebar{margin-top:6px}
}
```
But tile font-size set by calc(var(--tile)*.4)=20.8 automatically; no need override. Board `--tile: min(52px, ...)`; set `--tile:52px`. 4*52+3*8=232. Fine.

Height content: 14+54+52+16+44+32+14 + gaps 6*6=36 + padding 4 ≈ 266 + header ~58 = 324 < 390. Good. Could keep tiles 64 and target 60; 4*64+24=280. Content 14+60+64+16+46+34+14+36=284; header 58 →342 < 390. Good. Use tile 60, target 58.

But the landscape screenshot is at 844 wide; app max 680, content centered. With compact sizes, fine.

Also landscape start overlay: panel 458 tall > 390 and scrolls; button visible but "How to play" below; acceptable. Could compact the hero on low heights: reduce logo, demo margins. There's a `@media (max-height:700px)` that sets target 64, demo margins, hides footnote, but not overlay. The start screenshot shows panel extends beyond bottom with scroll; still usable. Maybe reduce panel paddings and logo size at max-height 500 to fit entirely:
```
